  "name": "Fachwerk: statically indeterminate truss with elastic bars",
  "description": "The same truss with an extra Stab D-C: 2 j = 10 < 8 members + 3 reactions, so equilibrium alone cannot say how the load is shared. Every Stab is an elastic bar with a cross section (I, T, L, H, square; one Young's modulus, 210 GPa), whose axial stiffness E A / L decides: the stiffer members carry more. The bars are steel beam-columns (they sag by their own weight and would buckle under enough compression); with the viscous damping of 5 / s everything settles within a second and the labels show the forces.",
